/--
Finite-measure threshold intersection arithmetic.  If the low-boundary set and
high-interface set are disjoint, their total measure cannot exceed the threshold
space.  Thus a strict size-sum surplus forces an intersection.  This is only the
measure arithmetic; PDE must still supply the size lower bounds.
-/
theorem thresholdSet_sizeSum_forces_intersection
    {lowBoundarySetMeasure highInterfaceSetMeasure thresholdSpaceMeasure : Real}
    (hsize : thresholdSpaceMeasure < lowBoundarySetMeasure + highInterfaceSetMeasure)
    (hdisjointUpper : lowBoundarySetMeasure + highInterfaceSetMeasure <= thresholdSpaceMeasure) :
    False := by
  linarith

/--
Size-sum version of the correlated high-low slice source.  It records a concrete
mechanism for `lowBoundarySetIntersectsHighInterfaceSet`: marginal lower bounds
on the cheap-boundary and high-interface threshold sets whose sum exceeds the
available threshold space.
